# Keep the deployment to what actually serves requests.
#
# None of this is imported by the application, but Vercel uploads every file in
# the repository unless told otherwise — and `supabase/` alone is ~250 KB of SQL
# that would sit in a serverless bundle doing nothing.
#
# EVERY PATTERN HERE MUST START WITH "/".
#
# This file uses .gitignore semantics, where an unanchored `supabase/` matches a
# directory of that name AT ANY DEPTH. Written without the leading slash it also
# deleted `lib/supabase/` — the Supabase clients the whole app imports — and the
# build died with "Can't resolve '@/lib/supabase/server'". The upload log is how
# you check this: it prints "Removed N ignored files", and N must equal the file
# count of the directories listed below and nothing more.

/legacy/
/supabase/
/scripts/
/docs/
/Claude outputs/

/Agents.md
/Design.md
/Goals.md
/Memory.md
/PRD.md
